# Caching & CDN Spec

## Scope

HTTP cache headers, CDN-safe page flows, static/upload caching, and generated
nginx cache behavior.

## Load when

Changing `utils.WriteJSON`, nginx generation, uploads/static serving, page route
resolution, Bible data loading, SSR, or CDN-facing behavior.

## Owns

- API cache headers: `backend/internal/utils/http.go`
- Runtime nginx generator: `internal/app/nginx.go`
- Frontend image nginx variant: `frontend/nginx/default.conf`
- Page flow: `.specs/route_resolution_spec`
- Bible client cache: `frontend/src/components/bible/api.ts`

## Contracts

| Layer | Contract |
| --- | --- |
| Go JSON APIs | `Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate` and `Pragma: no-cache` |
| Generated nginx API/config paths | no-store cache headers |
| `/uploads/*` | `public, max-age=2592000` (30 days) |
| Vite assets | hashed filenames; immutable-style static caching |
| WebSocket | not cacheable; upgrade proxied at `/ws` and `/api/ws` |
| SSR HTML | no-store; semantic route metadata uses tenant-scoped `seo:meta:v3:` Redis keys and is rendered against the validated canonical tenant origin |
| Sitemap XML | generated from canonical static routes plus public database content; tenant-scoped Redis cache for 15 minutes with mutation invalidation |
| Documentation APIs | no-store; route state is refreshed by scoped content-free WebSocket invalidation |
| KJV frontend reads | API remains `no-store`; one catalog promise plus an eight-book in-memory LRU and in-flight coalescing |
| Custom-page browse previews | API remains `no-store`; caller-safe previews use a 24-entry browser-memory LRU keyed by page id plus exact `updated_at` revision |

## SSR/SEO Cache Integrity

- Cached SEO values are raw title, description, image reference, favicon,
  site-name, route state, and side-effect-free image MIME metadata. Rendered HTML
  and request-derived origins are never cached.
- SEO resolution classifies authoritative success, genuine absence, optional
  degradation, and core dependency failure. Only success and absence enter
  Redis. Optional enrichment failure serves safe base metadata uncached; route
  or site-config failure returns uncached `503` with `Retry-After` and noindex.
- Redis reads are best-effort cache misses and Redis write failures do not alter
  the response. Malformed persisted branding/SEO config is a core failure, not
  an empty cacheable value.
- `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` is the canonical and sitemap origin. Existing tenants may
  derive it from their first valid `DOMAINS` entry during migration; production
  origins use HTTPS.
- Branding/SEO writes invalidate the tenant SEO namespace. Page, thread,
  product, and user create/update/delete paths invalidate their exact affected
  routes; `privacy`/`tos` pages also invalidate their root aliases, and user
  mutations also invalidate `/users`. Live stream metadata is resolved per SSR
  request because its in-memory state has no durable mutation invalidator.
- Documentation writes invalidate exact set/guide paths; public set/guide paths
  are discovered dynamically in the sitemap. Page, documentation, forum-thread,
  and product mutations also evict `/sitemap.xml`; transient database failures
  may serve the static route set but never cache that degraded result. Forum
  thread writes also invalidate their `/forum/docs/{categoryId}/{threadId}`
  presentation path.
- Missing recognized resources and unknown extensionless SPA paths return `404`
  plus HTML and `X-Robots-Tag` noindex. Authenticated/authentication routes remain
  renderable SPA shells but are noindex and absent from the sitemap.
- The SPA template is read from `INDEX_FILE_PATH` for every SSR response, using
  `frontend/dist/index.html` as the development fallback. Missing or unreadable
  templates are retried and return uncached `503`; hot-shipped replacements are
  visible without backend restart.
- SSR never fetches a page-, forum-, product-, or profile-controlled image URL.
  Dimensions belong to upload-time metadata; SSR may infer MIME from a safe file
  extension only.

## CDN-Safe Page Pattern

Landing page cold load must use:

1. `GET /pages/landing-slug`
2. `GET /pages/{slug}`

Reason: `/pages/index` is a single cache key that can point at different pages
over time. Per-slug fetches keep URL and resource identity aligned.

Live page changes bypass CDN through WebSocket:

- `page:update landing_page_changed` carries page identity only.
- `page:update page_updated` carries a content-free invalidation.
- `config:update landing_page_updated` carries `{ slug }` as a fallback/UI signal.

`GET /pages/browse` never transfers `pages.content`. Exact preview documents are
requested from `/pages/browse/{id}/preview` only after viewport and interaction
intent. They remain personalized, no-store responses and must not enter a CDN or
shared server cache.

The embedded KJV corpus is immutable, but `/api/bible/kjv/*` is not an exception
to the global API header policy. Reuse is process-local in the Go repository and
bounded to the browser session in the frontend client; corpus payloads are not
written to local storage.

## Anti-patterns

- Returning different resources from the same cacheable URL.
- Redirecting API endpoints for correctness.
- Relying on Cloudflare purge to make live data correct.
- Caching absolute SEO URLs by path without a validated canonical-origin key.
- Using Cloudflare HTML rewrites to repair origin-generated canonical/social URLs.
- Editing generated nginx config instead of `internal/app/nginx.go`.

